{
  "title": "Transfer centering with shared editor padding",
  "baselineCommit": "bdd340bba2db22b0c7f818d9d12cdb2436493d35",
  "sourceSha256": {
    "src/App.tsx": "e1c95aa43c80e153245776877ad75f2acafd107bf3e18aadeed6cbcb35e4da5a",
    "src/components/transfer/TransferWorkbench.tsx": "fbb8939d8b48740714acdb5d0b14b83f293a6cf8c2de09df85c5b09ff009f775"
  },
  "sourceFrozen": true,
  "method": [
    "Load the real Emerald and Quetzal saves through the browser file inputs, with genuine cached sprites and fonts.",
    "Measure actual viewport geometry after navigation without resetting page scroll for the measurements or desktop screenshots. Include entering transfer, returning from review, and reopening from a scrolled editor.",
    "The former transfer-only 40px desktop vertical padding caused avoidable document overflow for 707px Saves at 1366x768 and 1032px selection at 1440x1080. Use the shared editor 12px mobile/16px desktop minimum padding.",
    "Require equal top/bottom margins, zero scrollY and zero document overflow whenever the content and shared padding fit. Inspect overflow paths separately by scrolling to both ends only after recording the raw navigation state.",
    "Keep the documented four-Pokemon scenario: Aggron, Blaziken, Lotad and Marill into box 8 slots 24, 27, 28, 29.",
    "This run validates layout only. The earlier actual download and binary-preservation checks remain documented in transfer-centering.json; parser, conversion and save-writing code are unchanged."
  ],
